    "turn_text": "do that with a boat of the entire body. And so I heavily suspected at that point, but when the whip started to come down on me, on the democrat side said, okay, yeah, this is this is no. And that means that if if if I could have if I could have got through a hard lid on on what this ceiling could not exceed and eliminate the IRS 87,000 person army, And then that probably would have, that probably would have done it because there are some cuts. It is limited to a 1% cap per year for six years. That's not nothing. Unfortunately, it's over this year and this is an inflated spending year, Nate, because of COVID at all the excess monies that got appropriated for COVID this COVID that we wanted this backed up to pre-COVID spending levels where the starting base was. That didn't happen. And so I don't know. Even with the other stuff, we may not have been able to have done it at the end of the day. But yesterday afternoon, it became pretty clear when the Democrats started the whip. No, I'm not doing this.",
